          "id": "prt_002d",
          "sessionID": "ses_28",
          "messageID": "msg_002",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I wouldn't just retry until green - a test that fails intermittently almost always points at a real timing or race condition, like an unresolved promise or shared state between tests. Retrying just hides the bug; it'll resurface for someone else later, probably at a worse time. Worth spending a few minutes finding the actual cause first - both failures above mention 'timeout waiting for seed', which is a good lead."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_002e",
          "sessionID": "ses_28",
          "messageID": "msg_002",
          "type": "step-finish",
